<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caelius Vibenna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Caeles Vibenna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caelian-hill">Caelius</a> Vibenna (Etruscan Caile Vipinas) was an Etruscan warrior leader of the 6th century BCE from Vulci, who appears with his brother Aulus in Roman tradition and Etruscan art. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francois-tomb">François Tomb</a> shows him being freed from captivity by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mastarna">Macstrna</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> held that the Caelian Hill was named after him.</p></div>
